At 320, topbar fits (brand N, room chip, ?, ♪, ROOMS, LOG) but room code chip is close. The board is tiny (zones ~43x52), cards very tiny. The hand horizontally scrolls (5th card cut). Still works. Controls/hint area is hidden? In screenshot, between LP bar and hand there's no hint/END TURN visible! Wait, at 320x568, the board + LP bar ends around y=444; hand starts y=460. The controls row (hint + end turn) is missing/clipped. Let's check. The arena total height: side×2 + midline + controls. Available shell height = 568 - 52 - 126 (max380 handbar) = 390. Arena board height ~370? controls likely clipped by overflow hidden. The screenshot shows no "TAP A CARD..." / END TURN. That's a problem on very small screens: player can't end turn except keyboard (E) or auto-end. Need ensure controls visible.

At 320x568, the footer is 126px, top 52 → 390 shell. Board width: 320-10-6=304; zones (304-15)/6=48.2, height 57.8; each side: padding 6 + duelist 38 + 2 rows 115.6 + gaps 8 = 167.6; two sides 335 + midline 36 = 371 + controls 30 = 401 + arena-wrap padding 3 → 404 > 390. Clipped by overflow hidden. Need reduce board size for short screens or hide controls inside arena. We can add a height-based media query:
```css
@media (max-height: 620px) {
 .arena { width: min(100%, 58vh); }
 .handbar{height:112px}
 ...
}
```
But at 320x568, 58vh=329 > width 304; no effect (width-limited). The board's height is width-driven. To fit 390 height, board width must shrink to ~ (390 - 36 -30)/ (4 rows*1.2 + ~?) . Each side ~ 38+2*1.2w+...; total height ≈ 2*(38+2.4w+?) +36+30. Solve 2*(38+2.4w+14)+36+30=390 → 76+4.8w+28+66=390 → 4.8w=220 → w=46. So arena width ≈ 6*46+15+6=297. Current 304 → slightly too big. Set arena width 94%? Or reduce topbar/handbar heights.

Better: for small heights, hide the controls hint row and place END TURN as a floating button? The mobile hand-side is hidden, so need a button. Could show a compact fixed "END TURN" button overlaying bottom right of arena or top. But controls clipping indicates total height still over. Could reduce handbar to 112 and topbar 48; shell 408; then board+controls 404 fits. At 320x568, hand cards 64x90 need 112 height (padding). Good. Set `@media (max-height: 640px) { .handbar{height:112px;} }` but then card 90 + padding 8 = 98 fits. Also `.hand-card` width 64 gives 90 height. Good. topbar 52 remains. Shell 568-52-112=404; board+controls ~404. Just fits. But screenshot currently handbar 126 (max-width 380 rule), so change that rule to 112 and card 62. Then shell 404. Board 371 + controls 30 + padding 3 = 404. Exact. Might still clip 1-2px. Reduce board via side gap etc. Could also hide the `hint` on max-height 600 and make controls only END TURN with height 26, freeing. Actually hint is useful but can be omitted on tiny screens; END TURN still needed. Set `.controls .hint{display:none}` when max-height 620; controls 30. Board 371+30=401 < 404. Good. But then the player may not know what to do; top-level hint not critical. Or make hint absolute? Simpler hide only on shorts.

Also hand side is hidden on mobile; keep only controls END TURN.

Add:
```css
@media (max-height: 640px) {
  .handbar { height: 112px; }
  .hand-card { width: 62px; }
  .hand-scroll{padding-top:6px}
  .controls{min-height:26px}
  .controls .hint{display:none}
}
```
At 320x568 with max-width380 handbar 126 → overridden to 112. Good.

But the 380 media rule sets `.hand-card{width:64px}`, the max-height rule later if placed after will set 62. Order matters. Place at end after max-width rules. We'll add before reduced-motion at end.

At 390x844 it's unaffected.

Also at 320, topbar room chip code "24-BWYH" plus buttons fits, though tight. Fine.

Let's add. Also maybe set `.arena-wrap` overflow visible? No, then it overlaps hand. Better fit.

Add to CSS.

